WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.020
Most AI assistants take notes with a tool.

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:07.600
Mid-answer, the model stops, calls the tool, waits for the result, then starts again.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:10.240
Every note costs a full extra round trip.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.220
Fine in a demo. At scale, you feel it.

00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.160
So don't give it a tool. Give it a convention.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:21.220
The model writes its notes inline, inside the answer it's already writing, between two tags.

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.420
A tiny parser watches the stream.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:26.780
Open tag: start recording. Close tag: done.

00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:31.460
No tool call. No round trip. The model never breaks stride.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.120
And the notes land in the chat history, right where the reasoning happens.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:36.820
Working memory, for free.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.560
Tip one: tag your own notes.
